 r←LinkURLs text
⍝ Returns `text` with every URL in it turned into a link. `text` must be escaped already.
⍝ A full stop or a comma right after a URL is taken to end the sentence rather than to belong
⍝ to the URL. Used for what a package's author says when deprecating it, which typically points
⍝ to the successor.
 r←'(https?://[^\s<>"]*[^\s<>".,;:)])'⎕R'<a href="\1">\1</a>'⊣text
⍝Done
